:: Heist Wren Approach
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Wren>><<person1>>

You draw Wren away from the card table. One of <<his>> friends grumble at the interruption, but <<he>> lifts a hand without even looking back, and the grumbling dies down into a few sour looks.
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">><<He>> looks you over, expression softening. "Last time I saw you, you were in a rather more delicate condition. You've recovered well."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">><<He>> tips <<his>> head, a sly grin tugging at <<his>> mouth. "I remember the catsuit. Bold choice. Very you."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">><<He>> raises an eyebrow. "Prison did not break you, then. Good. You'll need that sort of backbone for what I have in mind."
<<elseif $wrenSeen?.length>><<He>> studies you for a moment, then lets out a laugh. "Oh, wow. What's the hurry?"
<<else>><<He>> regards you with curiosity, taking you in from head to toe. "So you're the one Landry's been going on about."<</if>>
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"I need your help," you say, the words leaving you in a rush before you can dress them up. "It's about the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You glance aside, then force yourself to meet <<his>> eyes. "Landry said you might help with something. The bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"Sorry to drag you away from your game," you say. "Landry sent me. It's about the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You flash Wren a bright smile. "Sorry, darling, but this can't wait. Landry sent me, and it concerns the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	"I was told to come to you," you say. "Landry thinks you can help with the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "We've got a bank to rob, and I need to know if you're in."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "Try not to look too flattered. We need you for the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"So... how do you feel about robbing a bank?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "We're planning something big. The bank."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren React]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren React
<<effects>>
For a moment Wren says nothing. Surprise flashes first, then calculation, then a bright, dangerous sort of amusement. By the time <<he>> speaks, fascination has settled neatly over everything else.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"Rob a bank," <<he>> repeats, a grin spreading across <<his>> face. "I was wondering when someone would finally say it to me outright."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"The bank." <<He>> lets out a low whistle. "Straight to the point. I respect that."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"The bank," <<he>> echoes, as though savouring the sound of it. "Very civil way to open a criminal conversation."
<<else>>
	"The bank. As in the only bank in this city that matters. The one with connections that reach all the way up to..." 
	<<He>> trails off and whistles under <<his>> breath. "That bank."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> folds <<his>> arms and begins to pace. <<His>> eyes are bright with interest now.
<br><br>
"Landry's been talking about that place for years. Never had anyone stupid enough to actually try it." <<He>> catches your eye and smiles. "That's a compliment, by the way."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren React 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren React 2
<<effects>>
<<He>> lifts one finger. "Before we go anywhere near that vault, we need intelligence. Real intelligence. Not Landry's stories after a drink too many."
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">>
	<<He>> smirks. "I've seen you move. You've got the instincts for this. Quick hands, quicker head. But instinct on its own gets people caught. We need observation."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">>
	"You got through prison. That tells me you can keep your head down, keep your mouth shut, and notice more than you let on. That's exactly what I need from you."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">>
	<<He>> pauses, something softer passing over <<his>> face before it vanishes again. "Last time we crossed paths, things were complicated. Fine. Leave it there. I still know you're tougher than you look, and I need that."
<<else>>
	<<He>> gives you a long, measuring look. "I hope you're as competent as Landry says you are."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen to Wren's plan|Heist Wren Plan]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Plan
<<effects>>
"Here's what you're going to do." Wren holds up <<his>> hand to points. "You'll visit the bank as a customer. Make a deposit, make a withdrawal, ask some pointless question at the counter, whatever normal people do."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans in, voice dropping.
<br><br>
"While you're there, you watch. You watch everything. Guard positions. Camera angles. Which doors need keycards and which ones open on a word and a smile. When the tellers swap over. How long security takes to react when something goes wrong. Every habit, every pattern, every careless little flaw."
<br><br>
<<He>> straightens and raises <<his>> hand again. "Seven visits. <span class="red">But do not go too often.</span> The guards are not idiots. Space your visits out. If you feel eyes on you, leave at once and come back another day... or week."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Plan 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Plan 2
<<effects>>
<<He>> fixes you with a steady look. "If you stir up too much suspicion, they'll bar you from the premises. Then we're back at the start, and I hate repeating myself."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	You swallow. "And if they catch me watching?"
	<br><br>
	"Then you'll wish all they did was ban you," <<he>> says, matter-of-fact. The edge in <<his>> voice lasts only a moment before it softens. "But you'll manage. Just act natural."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"And if they notice?" you ask, quieter than you meant to.
	<br><br>
	Wren's mouth twitches. "Then you leave before they decide to make it a problem. You're there to notice them, not the other way round."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"So seven visits, well spaced, and no lingering," you say. "Understood."
	<br><br>
	"Exactly." <<He>> smiles, pleased. "See? Much easier when someone listens."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Seven visits to a bank," you say. "You do know how to show a person a thrilling evening."
	<br><br>
	"Save the performance for the lobby," <<he>> says, amused. "Right now I need you forgettable."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You nod once. "Seven visits. Watch everything. Leave if it feels wrong."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> taps two fingers against <<his>> arm. "That sort of discipline keeps people alive."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"Seven visits. Spaced out. No mistakes," you say.
	<br><br>
	"That's the spirit." <<He>> grins. "You make it sound almost professional."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Seven visits to the dullest building in town," you say. "You really know how to spoil a person."
	<br><br>
	"And yet here you are." <<He>> smiles back without missing a beat. "Go and be dull enough to pass."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"Seven visits to the most boring building in the city," you say. "Thrilling."
	<br><br>
	"Says the person who agreed to rob it." <<He>> grins. "Now go be boring. Boringly observant."
<<else>>
	You nod. "Seven visits. Space them out. Don't get noticed."
	<br><br>
	"Quick study. I like that."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.wrenRecruited to true>>
<span class="gold"><i>Wren has joined the heist.</i></span><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Estate]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Bank Observation
<<run setup.hbsc.ensureState()>><<effects>><<bankHeistObservation>>
<<set _heist to $xchange.bankHeist>><<set _obs to _heist.observationDays>>
<<if setup.hbsc.isBanned()>>
	<<set _banDays to setup.hbsc.getBanRemainingDays()>>
	You step inside the bank, but before you can settle in, a guard approaches. 
	"We've noticed you've been glancing around to where you shouldn't. The management has asked that you refrain from visiting for a while. For your own comfort."
	<br><br>
	You are escorted back out to the street before you can so much as open your mouth.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You've been banned from the bank for <<print _banDays>> more day<<if _banDays isnot 1>>s<</if>>. Your observation progress has been reset.</span>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _heistVisitType is "sameDay">>
	You walk into the bank again, only to realise there is nothing new to learn from a second visit on the same day. The same guards loiter where they did before, the same tellers work behind the counters, and the same cameras stare down.
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			But a guard near the entrance is already watching you. <span class="red">You need to stay away for a while.</span>
		<<else>>
			One of the guards glances your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>><br><br>
	<span class="purple">Visiting the bank twice in one day is reckless.</span>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _heistVisitType is "consecutive">>
	You join the queue and try to look like any other customer, but you were here yesterday and the place has not forgotten your face. The tellers are the same. The guards are the same.
	<br><br>
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			A guard near the entrance is watching you with focused stare. <span class="red">You're drawing significant attention</span>,
		<<else>>
			You catch a guard glancing your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention</span>,
		<</if>>
		making you remember
	<</if>>
	Wren's warning echoes in your head. <i>Back-to-back days will flag you.</i>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	/* Valid observation - spaced properly */
	You step into the bank and take your place in the queue. Marble gleams under the lights. Polished brass catches at the corners of your vision. You keep your face blank and your posture loose while your eyes keep moving.
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			But a guard near the entrance is watching you with a stare that keeps returning no matter where you stand. <span class="red">You're drawing significant attention. You should space your visits further apart.</span>
		<<elseif _heist.suspicion gte 5>>
			You notice a guard glance your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention. Consider spacing your visits out more.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _obs is 1>>
		Your first visit teaches you the shape of the place. Two visible cameras cover the public floor, one above the entrance and one aimed across the teller windows. Three armed guards work the room. Behind the counter sits a service door with a keycard reader beside it.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 1/7: Floor layout noted.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 2>>
		On the second visit you come at a different hour and watch the guards instead of the counters. One stays by the entrance, one walks across the lobby, and one remains near a small desk at the back. The roaming guard passes the service door every four minutes with near-perfect regularity.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 2/7: Guard rotation pattern identified.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 3>>
		Third visit. The cameras leave a weak spot by the eastern wall, where a decorative pillar breaks the angle. The service door opens twice while you wait, and through it you catch a glimpse of a staircase leading down.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 3/7: Camera blind spot and basement access located.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 4>>
		Fourth visit. A man in an expensive suit arrives and is ushered through the service door without going near a teller. The guard at the back desk lets <<him>> pass after a brief exchange. No keycard. No paperwork. Probably some sort of spoken code.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 4/7: VIP access procedure observed.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 5>>
		Fifth visit. You time the shift change. At one-thirty, the roaming guard is replaced. For roughly thirty seconds, both guards vanish into the break room corridor.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 5/7: Shift change window identified.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 6>>
		Sixth visit. You study the electronic lock on the service door more closely. It uses an older magnetic strip reader, the sort Wren could probably bypass in <<nnpc_his "Wren">> sleep. You also spot a maintenance hatch near the restrooms that likely opens onto the building's utility corridor.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 6/7: Lock type and alternate access route catalogued.</span>
	<<elseif _obs gte 7>>
		Seventh visit. You go over every detail again until the bank feels etched behind your eyes. Guard positions. Camera coverage. The shift change window. The magnetic lock. The maintenance hatch. The staircase down towards the vault.
		<br><br>
		You have everything you need.
		<br><br>
		<span class="gold">Observation complete. Report back to Wren.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Wren>><<person1>>
You pull Wren aside again. By now <<his>> friends seem almost resigned to it, though a few still send dirty looks your way.
<br><br>
You lay out everything you saw. The floor plan. The guard rotations. The camera blind spot. The shift change window. The magnetic locks. The maintenance hatch.
<br><br>
Wren listens without interrupting, head tilted slightly, eyes fixed on you. When you finish, <<he>> is quiet. Then <<he>> grins. "You're good at this. Better than I expected."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Observation 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation 2
<<effects>>
Wren starts pacing, building speed as the pieces fit together in <<his>> head.
<br><br>
"The maintenance hatch is our way in. It should connect to the utility corridor, and that corridor ought to run alongside the vault staircase. I can bypass the magnetic locks. Those old strip readers have a known weakness."
<br><br>
<<He>> stops and turns back to you. "The shift change window is our golden thirty seconds. That's when we move from the utility corridor to the staircase.
After that, we're in the dark. Literally. The vault level has its own power supply and its own security."
<<if $skulduggery gte 600>><<He>> smiles. "With your skills, I like our odds."
<<elseif $skulduggery gte 400>><<He>> tilts <<his>> head. "It will be tight, but it can be done."
<<else>><<His>> expression grows more serious. "It's going to be dangerous. Make sure you're ready."<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Observation 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation 3
<<effects>>
Wren folds <<his>> arms and leans back against the wall.
<br><br>
"I can handle the physical side. Locks, doors, getting us in and out. But the electronic security on the vault level?" <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "Not my field. <span class="teal">We need our little friend at the pub</span> to look over this mapping. They can work out the electronic layout and tell us how not to die in it."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"You mean M-Mickey?" you ask quietly.
	<br><br>
	"Don't say their name out loud," <<he>> says, though <<hes>> smiling. "But yes. Bring what you've got to the pub. Landry can pass it along."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"The one at the pub?" you ask, lowering your voice on instinct.
	<br><br>
	"That's the one." <<He>> smiles faintly. "See? You do know how to be discreet."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"The pub, then," you say. "I'll make sure it gets to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> nods. "The sooner they see it, the sooner we can move."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"So I carry secrets to the pub and pretend I'm not enjoying myself," you say.
	<br><br>
	"Yes," <<he>> says dryly. "Try the pretending part especially hard."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You nod. "I'll take it to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> pushes off the wall. "Simple jobs are the ones people mess up by overthinking them."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"The pub. Fine. I'll get it done," you say.
	<br><br>
	"That's what I like to hear." <<He>> grins. "Quick and clean."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"So I get to play courier again," you say. "How glamorous."
	<br><br>
	"Call it a vital part of the operation," <<he>> says. "Though I know you prefer jobs with an audience."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"So I get to play courier again," you sneer. "Wonderful."
	<br><br>
	"Think of it as networking." <<He>> grins. "Now go. The sooner they see this mapping, the sooner we move."
<<else>>
	You nod. "The pub. I'll get it to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good. The sooner they see this, the sooner we move."
<</if>>
<br><br><<set $xchange.bankHeist.wrenReported to true>>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.suspicion to null>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.lastObservationDay to null>>
<<link [[Are you nervous?|Heist Wren Report Nervous]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Nervous
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"A-Are you nervous?" you ask quietly.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You hesitate, then ask, "You are nervous too, aren't you?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"May I ask something?" you say. "Are you nervous about this?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Tell me honestly," you say. "Are you nervous, or are you merely build up suspense?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"You look steady enough," you say. "But are you nervous?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"What, you're not even a little scared?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Are you nervous about this?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Wren's expression stills, and what sits underneath it looks a good deal more honest.
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">>
	"I've broken into a lot of places. Worn a lot of disguises." <<He>> smiles faintly. "But nothing like this. This one matters."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">>
	"I've been locked up before. I know what it feels like. And I know what kind of place this bank is." <<He>> meets your eyes. "So yes. A little."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">>
	"I've seen enough to know things don't always go to plan." <<His>> face is difficult to read. "But we go anyway. That's the work."
<<else>>
	"Nervous? No. Nervous is for people who have something to lose. I'm..." <<He>> searches for the word. "Alert."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Nervous 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Nervous 2
<<effects>>
Wren straightens, the confession gone as quickly as it came. "See you on the other side."
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Estate]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
